# =============================================================================
# Store — GET BY ID requests (VS Code REST Client) — GET /api/v1/stores/{id} (ADMIN)
# =============================================================================
# How to run:
#   1. Start the backend: `docker compose up -d --build` — http://localhost:4000
#   2. Click the "Send Request" CodeLens above any request below.
#
# Prerequisites: an admin persona (see http/store/create.http header for the
# SQL promotion one-liner).
#
# Notes:
#   - Run top-to-bottom on first use — later requests assume earlier ones ran.
#   - All data is FAKE. The automated suite: StoreApiTests (src/test/java).
#   - Access tokens expire after 15 MINUTES. If tokened requests suddenly 401,
#     re-send request 1 (admin login) to refresh the chained tokens, then continue.
#   - Re-running: requests 2 and 11 return 409 (brand/email persist) — harmless.
#   - Expected codes: 200 found, 401 no/invalid token, 403 non-admin, 404 unknown
#     id, 204 delete, 500 known wart for non-UUID paths (see request 10).
# =============================================================================

@storeUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/stores
@authUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth

### 1 — Setup: login the admin persona
# Expected: 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2 — Setup: create a store to fetch
# Expected: 201
# @name createStore
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Gettable Store",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{adminLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "12 Market Road, Lagos",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "gettable-store@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 3 — Fetch by publicId
# Expected: 200 — brand "Gettable Store", createdAt/updatedAt present
GET {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4 — Unknown id
# Expected: 404 — "Store not found"
GET {{storeUrl}}/99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 5 — No Authorization header
# Expected: 401
GET {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}

### 6 — Garbage token
# Expected: 401
GET {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-jwt

### 7 — Setup: signup a regular persona
# Expected: 201 (409 if she already exists — either way the account exists)
# @name regularSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Bola Getless",
  "email": "bola.getless@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234569"
}

### 8 — Setup: login the regular persona
# Expected: 200
# @name regularLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bola.getless@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 9 — Fetch as a regular user
# Expected: 403 — by-id reads are admin-only
GET {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{regularLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 10 — Non-UUID path segment
# Expected: 500 — KNOWN WART: MethodArgumentTypeMismatchException hits the
# catch-all handler (parked hardening item from the security audit; the suite
# pins the UUID paths, not this one). Documented, not fixed.
GET {{storeUrl}}/not-a-uuid
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 11 — Setup: create a second store, then soft-delete it
# Expected: 201
# @name createDoomed
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Doomed Get Store",
  "storeType": "KIOSK",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{adminLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "12 Market Road, Lagos",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "doomed-get@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 12 — Soft-delete it
# Expected: 204
DELETE {{storeUrl}}/{{createDoomed.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 13 — Fetch the deleted store
# Expected: 200 with status DELETED — the soft-delete contract: the row survives
GET {{storeUrl}}/{{createDoomed.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
